Applies the policy text drafted in
agl-manifest/ai-office/reports/approvals/2026-10-12-fashionfactory-privacy-policy.md
to docs/privacy-policy.html, and changes the privacy_policy_test.dart
assertions that encode the old (2.x) policy in the same commit, as the QA
review required:

- "Android requests only INTERNET": expected set is now
  {INTERNET, RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED} (the source manifest since 3.0.0), and the
  page must name INTERNET, RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED, POST_NOTIFICATIONS, VIBRATE.
- api.fashionfactory.americangroupllc.com: flipped to assert the host is
  ABSENT from the policy (the gateway client is gone), and that the page says
  the app's own features make no network requests.
- "the page documents no key the app does not store": now checks the 3.0.0
  key pattern fashionfactory.<what>.vN and requires at least one match
  (previously it matched only v2 keys and would have passed vacuously).
- "the v1 keys are still read" -> "the 2.x and 1.x keys are deleted on
  upgrade": asserts all six legacy keys are named in the store's clear list
  and that the page says they are deleted, not carried across.
- "Shop buttons leave the app" -> "opening a saved link leaves the app".
- "what an affiliate tag identifies" -> "the policy makes no affiliate claim,
  because the app has none" (affiliate tagging was removed with the catalog
  in 0fcbad3; lib/ and the page must not mention it).
- New: "the policy describes where ads appear as the code places them"
  (AglAdBanner only in home_screen.dart and brand_screen.dart, no
  interstitial; the page says so).

Beyond the draft's wording: the header subtitle "Fashion, bags & footwear
deals" becomes "Your clothing orders, sizes and return dates"; the orders row
also names the exchanged-from link that Order.toJson stores; "Reminder
timing" is written as the UI's actual label "Return reminders"; "Delete all
data does the same" is written as what clearAll() does (orders, settings,
reminders; not the IABTCF consent keys).

